{# THE PROVENANCE STRIP — one line, at the head of the page.

   It was the whole source card once: the record's own words, its position in the
   observation page's notation, its time and a strip of 76px thumbnails. Its job
   was never to be READ — 76px is enough to prove a photograph exists and not
   enough to see what is in one — and now that the RAIL carries the same record
   legibly ({@see @UhifadhiIncident/report/_observation.html.twig}), a second copy
   of the words, the position and the thumbnails above the form is duplication on
   the one page a filer is trying to get through.

   So what is left is the two things a strip is for: it says which record this
   filing came from, and it links back to it. Nothing on it is editable —
   provenance is written once, at filing, and never again.

   Parameters: prefill, files
   ========================================================================== #}
<section class="i-src" data-incident-source-card>
    <div class="hd">{{ ux_icon('incident:git-branch') }}<b>Filed from {{ prefill.label }}</b>
        {% if prefill.backUrl %}<a class="go" href="{{ prefill.backUrl }}">Open the source →</a>{% endif %}</div>

    <p class="i-srcnote">
        {%- if files is not empty -%}
            its words, its position, its time and its {{ files|length }} photograph{{ 1 == files|length ? '' : 's' }}
            are in the rail, at a size that can be read
        {%- else -%}
            its words, its position and its time are in the rail, at a size that can be read
        {%- endif -%}
        · its category guess, coordinates, time and note are already in the form below · the link is kept forever
    </p>
</section>
